            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac diseases in people with intellectual disability.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>515-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">In people with ID there is more morbidity than in the general population, including cardiac diseases. Dutch figures on this subject are scarce.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Descriptive study of the prevalence of cardiac diseases in 436 residential clients in Echt, the Netherlands, and comparisons between men and women, age groups, and level and aetiology of ID, were carried out.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">It was found that the total prevalence of cardiac diseases was 14%, with a higher prevalence among women, the elderly, and people with mild/moderate ID.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The prevalence of cardiac diseases in residential clients is substantial. With the increasing number of ageing people with ID and people with ID living more independently in community-integrated residences, it is expected that the morbidity and mortality from cardiac diseases will increase further.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
